                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22440e8a-dec6-37a3-87cc-3c35b9535caa",
                        "entry_id": "7c9d77c7-6768-3e66-9ba9-1f12cc68f896",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à l’hétéronormativité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7213007b-c839-3e35-926d-0f4f00f75f2d",
                        "entry_id": "7c9d77c7-6768-3e66-9ba9-1f12cc68f896",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui considère l’hétérosexualité comme l'unique orientation sexuelle à suivre, comme une orientation sexuelle normale ou comme une orientation sexuelle supérieure aux autres (saphisme, bisexualité...)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47096e45-fc08-4b12-bfba-f06bfd9d7270",
                                "sense_id": "7213007b-c839-3e35-926d-0f4f00f75f2d",
                                "text": "En plus, je trouve que l’homme a l’obligation d’organiser la soirée la plus romantique de sa vie et la fille, celle de porter des dessous affriolants très peu confortables (tout ça est très hétéronormatif)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "44fa74b6-1689-3170-b037-de1cff591651",
                        "entry_id": "7c9d77c7-6768-3e66-9ba9-1f12cc68f896",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui suit les valeurs ou les codes hétérosexuels dominants dans la société."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "288cafa7-87fd-4461-9ab9-89bb25e446a0",
                                "sense_id": "44fa74b6-1689-3170-b037-de1cff591651",
                                "text": "Cette fonction déjoue la censure qui jette tout ce qui n’est pas hétéronormatif hors du dicible et donc, hors de l’espace social."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ca22b8bb-895f-4400-a05d-08da8ceec845",
                        "source_entry_id": "7c9d77c7-6768-3e66-9ba9-1f12cc68f896",
                        "target_lang_word": "heteronormative",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "heteronormative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                        "entry_id": "17b239c3-67c3-3bdf-b05e-f6b5179bf142",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to the practices and institutions that privilege or value heterosexuality, heterosexual relationships, and traditional gender roles as fundamental and \\\"natural\\\" within society."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "544af3b6-4f65-4fa5-8fc9-08af402d0d22",
                                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                                "text": "Much of the language used when discussing wedding planning is heteronormative, which can alienate homosexual couples."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72c1dd44-9279-4430-872e-331f05112c93",
                                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                                "text": "This suggests both that film studies can be heteronormative even when it is analyzing homosexual representations and that close textual analysis is itself structured by heterosexual presumptions and assumptions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "957fad1f-828d-4726-a20a-e6d78fa4f9a7",
                                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                                "text": "In the same way, homosexuality and bisexuality will always be seen as problematic in heteronormative organizations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "227fa638-ec75-47d1-88f5-a86c9f7bf015",
                                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                                "text": "Homonationalism needs to be more broadly understood as one dimension of “homonormativity,” which Lisa Duggan described over a decade ago as a gay mindset that does not “contest dominant heteronormative assumptions and institutions but upholds and sustains them.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "81391308-fd21-4290-835d-5162f220e944",
                        "source_entry_id": "7c9d77c7-6768-3e66-9ba9-1f12cc68f896",
